Rebased onto the latest `main` and resolved the conflicts.

@hnyls2002 @ch-wan — this is a pure refactor with no behaviour change: it unifies the HiSparse device-pool mapping internals that were duplicated across the allocator and the memory-pool paths, netting out a few lines shorter. Nothing to validate beyond CI staying green.

**On the red checks:** they're all `pr-gate` / `pr-test-*-finish` failing because the PR has no `run-ci` label — no test has actually run. I'm not in `.github/CI_PERMISSIONS.json`, so I can't trigger it myself. Could a maintainer add the label (or `/tag-and-rerun-ci`)?

@xiezhq-hermann could you re-review `360a8228c21c` and enable `run-ci` for the HiSparse mapping paths? Your requested main integration and consolidated device-pool selection are included. The recorded focused CPU checks pass 16 tests with 11 subtests; fused GPU dispatch was mocked and still needs upstream validation.

There is also an old failing title check. The current title is `[Refactor] hisparse: unify device-pool mapping and selection`, matching the check's required format. I attempted to rerun workflow 40240035123 on the unchanged head, but GitHub rejected it with “Must have admin rights to Repository.” Could you rerun that check along with the authorized CI, or advise if a different title is needed?

Please let me know if any further implementation changes are needed before approval.

